<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine central bank sells dlrs at 29 pesos.</title>
<headline>Philippine central bank sells dlrs at 29 pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine central bank was selling dollars at 29 pesos in early trading, traders said on Thursday..</p>
<p>Volume was still limited at $500,000 per transaction, they said.  </p>
<p>The peso had so far traded in the range of 29/29.45 to the dollar after opening at 29.26. Volume was modest at $11 million after an hour of trading.</p>
<p>The central bank has been selling dollars since Monday at 29 pesos ever since it allowed on Friday to let the peso move in a wider range.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8937</p>
